commit: 52a842f1660c2988bd8ae957e01202a162ca4f0b

{"body":"Task 05 of t-393. In landscape the empty Today, History and Medications now sit 12 pt from the element their board\nmeasures from. Portrait values are untouched.\n\n### Problem\n\nt-383 set 12 pt for the empty-state top in landscape, but the visible gap came out at 45 pt on Today, 14 pt on History\nand 32 pt on Medications. The modifier's padding sits inside a list row, and the lists add their own space above it: a\n32 pt section gap on Today and a 16 pt top margin on Medications.\n\n### How it is solved\n\n- Each `EmptyStateTop` case holds its own compact value, so `emptyStateTop` swaps by height size class as before. The\n  shared `emptyStateTopCompact` token is gone.\n- A padding cannot go below zero, and a negative one clips the block (the mark's top was cut off in a test build). So\n  a second shared modifier, `emptyStateListOffset`, sits on the `List` of Today and Medications. In compact height,\n  while the block shows, it sets the section gap to 0, and on Medications it sets the top margin to 0 when the block\n  starts the list. The same calls run in every state and only their values change, so a turn keeps the list's state.\n- No screen holds a number. The call sites pass a case and two booleans.\n- The modifier has to sit before `blockGapBetweenSections` and `screenSpacing` on the list, because the call closest\n  to the list wins. The catalog line says so.\n\n### Each screen\n\nGap is the board element's bottom edge (frame from `axe describe-ui`) to the first visible pixel of the block (from the\nscreenshot, 3 px per pt, iPhone 17 Pro, iOS 26.5, turned with the Debug hook).\n\n| Screen | `emptyStateTop` compact | List offset given up | Measures from | Board measures from | Gap |\n|--------|-------------------------|----------------------|---------------|---------------------|-----|\n| Today, no chip | 11 pt | section gap 32 to 0 | date line | date line | 12.3 pt |\n| Today under the chip | 11 pt | section gap 32 to 0 | chip | chip | 12.3 pt |\n| History | 10 pt | none, it is a scroll view | top bar's bottom edge | large title | 12.3 pt |\n| Medications, no card | 8 pt | top margin 16 to 0, section gap 32 to 0 | top bar | top bar | 12.0 pt |\n| Medications, archived card | 8 pt | section gap 32 to 0 | archived card's bottom edge | top bar | 12.0 pt |\n\n- Landscape has no large title. The bar is inline, so History measures from the bar's bottom edge. The brief's \"about\n  25 pt\" for History was an estimate: I measured 14.3 pt at the old value of 12.\n- Before: Today 45.3 pt, History 14.3 pt, Medications 32 pt. Today's 46.3 pt ink to ink matches the brief's 47 pt.\n- The fractional gaps come from the symbol's and the mark's own padding inside their frames.\n\n### Checks by walk\n\n- The archived card keeps its place: Medications' `medication-row` is at y 94 before the archive and the Archived card\n  is at y 94 after it, 52 pt tall, ending at y 146. The block's first pixel is at y 158.\n- Mark and icon sizes are unchanged. Visible heights in landscape: the pills 44.7 pt (the same in portrait), the\n  History clock 34 pt (the same in portrait). Today's mark is 32 pt, 60% of its 53.4 pt in portrait, which is t-383's\n  `emptyStateMark`. This diff does not touch it.\n- At the largest Dynamic Type size in landscape the heading is on screen at rest on Today (y 211), History (y 168) and\n  Medications, and each screen scrolls to its end.\n- Look check: the brief names no design picture. I compared each screen's landscape screenshot with its portrait one\n  by eye for the mark, icon, text sizes and side insets, and only the top gap differs.\n\n### Shared pieces used\n\n`emptyStateTop`, `EmptyStateTop`, the new `emptyStateListOffset`, and `Spacing` tokens: `emptyTodayTopCompact`,\n`emptyTodayTopBelowChipCompact`, `emptyHistoryTopCompact`, `emptyMedicationsTopCompact`. `screenSpacing` and\n`blockGapBetweenSections` are unchanged.\n\n### Compromise\n\nThe two list values live in the modifier but restate `Spacing.blockGap` and `Spacing.firstBlockTop`, which\n`screenSpacing` sets too. If either token changes, the modifier follows it by name.\n"}
